stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PRESENTED: SG1 operator presents, bridge closes to zero
    PRESENTED --> APPROVED: SG2 approver decides with step-up, hash unchanged
    PRESENTED --> RETURNED: SG3 return with a reason code
    PRESENTED --> SUPERSEDED: SG4 reprocess, newer rule version, due date passes or role changes
    APPROVED --> LOCKED: SG5 lock while the approval is current
    APPROVED --> VOIDED: SG6 returned before lock, or SG7 portal object hash changed
    LOCKED --> [*]
    RETURNED --> [*]
    VOIDED --> [*]
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]

    note right of PRESENTED
        Blocking count must be zero to approve
        Maker, reviewer and portal performer are never eligible
        Escalation finds a backup, never the maker
    end note

    note right of RETURNED
        The next presentation is always a new artefact
        linked to this one
    end note
